(Bug #78: the same run-time guard, either side of the bound in one
 program. -1 bytes used to be accepted and reported `capacity -1` - the
 shape of bug #58 - while a size within the bound must go on working and
 must not leave the error flag raised behind it.)

a number called refused is arguments's first as a number.
a number called wanted is arguments's second as a number.

a buffer called wrong is refused bytes in size.
On error print "refused: {refused} bytes".
Print "wrong capacity: {wrong's capacity}".

a buffer called right is wanted bytes in size.
On error print "this line must not print".
Print "right capacity: {right's capacity}".

Set right to "hello".
Print "right holds: {right} ({right's size} bytes)".
